[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: SYS-ARI-001 · Acceptance criteria

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @requirements

[ACCEPTANCE_CRITERION]
UID: SYS-ARI-001.AC-1
STATEMENT: An addition request with operands "2" and "3" is answered with the result "5".
VERIF_LEVELS: system
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-ARI-001

[ACCEPTANCE_CRITERION]
UID: SYS-ARI-001.AC-2
STATEMENT: A subtraction request with operands "2" and "3" is answered with the result "-1".
VERIF_LEVELS: system
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-ARI-001

[ACCEPTANCE_CRITERION]
UID: SYS-ARI-001.AC-3
STATEMENT: A multiplication request with operands "2" and "3" is answered with the result "6".
VERIF_LEVELS: system
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-ARI-001

[ACCEPTANCE_CRITERION]
UID: SYS-ARI-001.AC-4
STATEMENT: A division request with operands "3" and "2" is answered with the result "1.5".
VERIF_LEVELS: system
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-ARI-001

[ACCEPTANCE_CRITERION]
UID: SYS-ARI-001.AC-5
STATEMENT: Operands with more digits than a 64-bit integer or a double can hold (at least 30 digits) give a result without any lost digit.
VERIF_LEVELS: system
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-ARI-001
